#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD9744 expect=noViolation domain=TS
# Rule:Description: Raise an error when the TS dataset contains a record with TSPARMCD='HLTSUBJI' and TSVAL='Y' (indicating a healthy-subjects study) but does not contain a record with TSPARMCD='INDIC' and TSVALNF='NA'.
#note "No HLTSUBJI=Y record exists so $HLTSUBJI=0 -> the leading conjunct is false; the INDIC record has no TSVALNF=NA so the second conjunct stays true, isolating the guard-false silent path"
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TS label="Trial Summary"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col TSPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Summary Parameter Short Name"
col TSVAL type=Char label="Parameter Value"
col TSVALNF type=Char label="Parameter Value Null Flavor"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | HLTSUBJI | N |
CDISCPILOT01 | TS | INDIC | Mild to Moderate Alzheimer's Disease |
---
